{"id": "mm7132e3", "attempt": "read", "status": "ok", "message_id": "msg_011Cg8GvijaAfKbs19NwDut9", "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "error_kind": "", "errors": [], "usage": {"input": 31918, "write_1h": 0, "write_5m": 0, "cache_read": 0, "output": 5920}, "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"text": "{\"id\":\"mm7132e3\",\"reader\":{\"model\":\"prod\",\"reader_id\":\"prod\",\"role\":\"judgment\"},\"data_focus\":{\"v\":\"yes\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"The percentage of locally acquired cases increased from 51% (33 of 65) during May 17–July 2 to 82% (145 of 175)\"}]},\"outcome_types\":[{\"v\":\"binary/categorical\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"Among 1,054 cases for which race and ethnicity were reported, 41% occurred among White persons, 28% among Hispanic persons\"}]},{\"v\":\"count/rate\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"the number of reported cases increased rapidly during this time\"},{\"loc\":\"figure 1\",\"q\":\"Monkeypox cases, by report date* — United States, May 17–July 22, 2022\"}]}],\"analytic_depth\":[{\"v\":\"summary\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"summary\",\"q\":\"Among U.S. monkeypox cases with available data, 99% occurred in men, 94% of whom reported recent male-to-male sexual or close intimate contact\"}]},{\"v\":\"comparison\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"the percentage of cases among Black persons increased from 12% (29 of 248) during May 17–July 2 to 31% (247 of 806)\"},{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"accounted for more than one half (54%) of monkeypox cases in persons for whom information on race and ethnicity is available\"}]}],\"procedures\":[],\"comparison\":{\"framework\":\"fixed referent\",\"scale\":null,\"referent\":\"share of Black and Hispanic persons in the general population (34%); historical reports of endemic monkeypox\",\"across\":[\"race/ethnicity\",\"period\",\"clinical presentation\"],\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"Black and Hispanic persons, who represent approximately one third (34%) of the general population\"},{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"Compared with historical reports of monkeypox in areas with endemic disease, currently reported outbreak-associated cases are less likely to have a prodrome\"}]},\"inference\":{\"v\":\"none\",\"method_stated\":false,\"ev\":[]},\"primary_measures\":[{\"v\":\"percentage\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"table 1\",\"q\":\"* Percentages calculated using nonmissing data.\"}]},{\"v\":\"number of cases\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"figure 1\",\"q\":\"Monkeypox cases, by report date* — United States, May 17–July 22, 2022\"}]}],\"regression_fields\":null,\"public_health_question\":{\"v\":\"What were the epidemiologic and clinical characteristics of U.S. monkeypox cases reported during May 17–July 22, 2022?\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"To describe epidemiologic and clinical characteristics, CDC analyzed case report form data for probable or confirmed cases\"}]},\"conditions\":[{\"v\":\"monkeypox\",\"role\":\"outcome\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"title\",\"q\":\"Epidemiologic and Clinical Characteristics of Monkeypox Cases — United States, May 17–July 22, 2022\"}]}],\"study_design\":[{\"v\":\"surveillance/descriptive\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"CDC analyzed case report form data for probable or confirmed cases\"}]}],\"data_source_type\":[{\"v\":\"CDC surveillance system\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"On June 3, 2022, CDC released a case report form for health departments to report monkeypox cases.\"}]}],\"data_source_named\":[{\"v\":\"CDC monkeypox case report form\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"CDC released a case report form for health departments to report monkeypox cases.\"}]},{\"v\":\"CDC emergency response common operating platform\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"figure 1\",\"q\":\"date of case data entry into CDC’s emergency response common operating platform.\"}]}],\"setting\":{\"v\":\"US national\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"a total of 2,891 U.S. monkeypox cases were reported by 43 states, Puerto Rico, and DC\"}]},\"vaccine_outcome_type\":null,\"equity\":{\"level\":2,\"level_reason\":\"Race/ethnicity shares of cases are reported by period and set beside the general-population share (54% vs 34%) and called disproportionate, but no difference or ratio is computed, so the side-by-side cap applies.\",\"level_confidence\":\"medium\",\"level_alternative\":{\"level\":3,\"reason\":\"The 54% vs 34% contrast with 'disproportionately affected' framing could be read as a quantified, interpreted disparity.\"},\"dimensions\":[{\"v\":\"race/ethnicity\",\"role\":\"stratifier\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"summary\",\"q\":\"racial and ethnic minority groups appear to be disproportionately affected\"},{\"loc\":\"table 1\",\"q\":\"Race and ethnicity (1,054) › Black, non-Hispanic\"}]},{\"v\":\"sexual orientation and gender identity\",\"role\":\"descriptor\",\"basis\":\"behavior\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"337 (94%) reported sex or close intimate contact with a man during the 3 weeks before symptom onset\"}]},{\"v\":\"sexual orientation and gender identity\",\"role\":\"descriptor\",\"basis\":\"self-identified\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"table 1\",\"q\":\"Gender identity (1,195) › Transgender woman\"}]},{\"v\":\"sex\",\"role\":\"descriptor\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"Nearly all (99%) persons with case report forms available were men (cisgender and transgender)\"}]},{\"v\":\"age\",\"role\":\"descriptor\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"Median age was 35 years (IQR = 30–41 years).\"}]}],\"determinants_of_health\":{\"v\":\"homophobia, stigma, and discrimination\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"require addressing challenges that include homophobia, stigma, and discrimination\"}]},\"equity_action\":{\"v\":false,\"ev\":[]},\"equity_measurement\":\"Referent is the general-population share of Black and Hispanic persons (34%); race/ethnicity missing for 141 of 1,195 cases; case report forms received for only 41% of cases, and jurisdictions lacking forms were more racially diverse.\"},\"groupwise\":[],\"uncertain_fields\":[\"comparison\",\"groupwise\",\"equity.level\",\"outcome_types\"],\"confidence\":\"medium\",\"notes\":\"Race/ethnicity results are case composition (shares by period and versus population share) with no outcome per group and no test, so no groupwise entry. Vaccination history of cases (14% previously vaccinated) is descriptive only; vaccine_outcome_type left null. The comparison with typical endemic monkeypox relies on cited historical reports.\",\"view_issues\":\"Stray parenthesis in 'After detection of the first U.S. monkeypox case)'.\"}", "type": "text"}]}